 read it:</strong> useful preparation for Week 7.</div><a href="https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/general_writing/mechanics/documents/new_sentence_clarity_10312025.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open Purdue Sentence Clarity PDF →</a></div><div class="resource-pro"><span class="res-tag">Writing types</span><h3>University of Sydney — Types of Academic Writing</h3><p>Distinguishes <strong>descriptive, analytical, persuasive and critical</strong> academic writing and the language purposes associated with each.</p><div class="why"><strong>Why read it:</strong> helps students understand that academic writing changes with purpose.</div><a href="https://www.sydney.edu.au/students/study-skills/writing/types-of-academic-writing.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open writing types resource →</a></div></div><p class="citation-note">External resources are supplementary. The course materials and assessment criteria define the language expectations used in this course.</p><div class="takeaway" style="margin-top:14px"><strong>Suggested starting point:</strong> start with the <strong>University of Sydney</strong> and <strong>Monash</strong> pages. Use <strong>Manchester Academic Phrasebank</strong> as a reference throughout the semester rather than memorising phrases.</div></section><section id="exit"><div class="head"><div><span class="label">108–118 minutes</span><h2>Rewrite + Exit Ticket</h2></div><p>End with one immediate language improvement and one <strong>specific target for Week 5</strong>.</p></div><div class="grid"><div class="task"><h3>Rewrite Two Sentences</h3><div class="prompt">A. The results were <strong>really bad</strong>.</div><textarea placeholder="Rewrite precisely and objectively..."></textarea><div class="prompt">B. We used <strong>some equipment</strong> to check the system.</div><textarea placeholder="Rewrite with more formal and precise language..."></textarea></div><div class="task"><h3>Exit Ticket</h3><p>Complete <strong>one specific sentence</strong>:</p><div class="exit-stem">By Week 5, I want to be able to <strong>________________________</strong> in my writing.</div><textarea placeholder="One measurable skill only, e.g. describe a graph using exact values and appropriate trend language."></textarea></div></div></section><section id="homework"><div class="head"><div><span class="label">118–120 minutes</span><h2>Formative Homework</h2></div><p>Revision practice; not the graded 5-mark homework.</p></div><div class="home"><h3>Revise Your Diagnostic Paragraph</h3><p>Produce a clean <strong>150-word version</strong> for Week 2. Before submitting, check that you:</p><ul><li>replace <strong>vague words</strong> with precise information;</li><li>remove clearly <strong>colloquial expressions</strong>;</li><li>maintain a <strong>formal and objective tone</strong>;</li><li>use <strong>accurate technical vocabulary</strong>;</li><li>quantify at least <strong>two details</strong> where appropriate;</li><li>correct obvious <strong>sentence and grammar problems</strong>.</li></ul><div class="submission"><strong>Submission:</strong><br/><strong>Format:</strong> one revised paragraph, approximately <strong>150 words</strong>; bring a <strong>PDF/DOCX file or printed copy</strong>.<br/><strong>Deadline:</strong><strong>before the start of Week 2</strong>.<br/><strong>Where:</strong><strong>bring it to the Week 2 class</strong> for collection/review.</div><p><strong>Keep both versions.</strong> We will use the Week 1 baseline and revised version later to show progress.</p></div></section><div class="completion"><div><strong>Week 1 complete?</strong><br/>Updates browser-local course progress.</div><button class="completebtn" id="complete">Mark Week 1 Complete</button></div></main><footer><strong>English for Master · Week 1</strong><br/>Academic English Foundations for MSc Electrical Engineering · University of Kufa</footer></div></div><script>const key='efm-progress-v1',completeBtn=document.getElementById('complete');let a=[];try{a=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key)||'[]')}catch(e){}function renderCompletion(){if(!completeBtn)return;if(a.includes(1)){completeBtn.textContent='Week 1 Completed ✓';completeBtn.classList.add('done')}else{completeBtn.textContent='Mark Week 1 Complete';completeBtn.classList.remove('done')}}if(completeBtn){completeBtn.onclick=()=>{a=a.includes(1)?a.filter(x=>x!==1):[...a,1];localStorage.setItem(key,JSON.stringify(a));renderCompletion()};renderCompletion()}</script></body></html>